          <strong>The Short Answer: Which Game Should You Play?</strong>
          While both games share a top-down pixel art extraction formula inspired by S.T.A.L.K.E.R. and Escape from Tarkov, <strong>Scavland is substantially darker, more hardcore, and mechanically deeper</strong>. It shifts away from arcade-style rogue-lite looting toward gritty survival sim mechanics: 300+ realistic weapon attachments, devastating gun malfunctions, dynamic anomaly fog (The Mist), and 10 living wasteland factions with shifting reputations.
