        <h2 id="development">Origin &amp; Design Heritage</h2>
        <p>In a detailed 6-year development retrospective published on the Steam Community, the lead developer of <strong>Scavland</strong> revealed that the team grew from 3 to 15 developers over half a decade. Rather than copying modern extraction shooters, Scavland pulls design DNA from legendary classics:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Tibia &amp; Ultima Online:</strong> Spatial awareness, unforgiving corpse-run economics, and open-ended wasteland interactions.</li>
          <li><strong>Darkwood:</strong> Psychological tension, field-of-view cone mechanics, and terrifying ambient night encounters.</li>
          <li><strong>Escape from Tarkov:</strong> Realistic weapon modding, chamber inspection, and detailed cartridge ballistics.</li>
          <li><strong>S.T.A.L.K.E.R. &amp; Metro:</strong> Bleak Eastern European post-cataclysm atmosphere, anomalous weather phenomena, and faction skirmishes.</li>
        </ul>

